/*******************************************************************************
 * CHIP:  BCMI_TSCBH_FE_GEN2_XGXS
 * REGISTER:  DSC_DCCAN_CTL1
 * BLOCKS:   DSC_F
 * REGADDR:  0xd0fb
 * DEVAD:    1
 * DESC:     DC canceller control register 1.
 * RESETVAL: 0x40 (64)
 * ACCESS:   R/W
 * FIELDS:
 *     DCC_EN           1 to enable dc canceller.
 *     DCC_KP           Gain of DC canceller loop.dcc_kp controls the overall gain of the DC canceller feedback loop.Valid values: {0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7}
 *     DCC_CTRL         Bandwidth of DC canceller.This controls the value on N in the Barchetta DC canceller:N = 3 + dcc_ctrl[2:0].Valid values: {0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7}
 *     DCC_TEST         test bits for DC Canceller.dcc_test[7] dcc_pk_en.Override the input to the BLW max amplitude block with a DC-CAN max amplitude signal instead.This allows DC-CAN specific signals to be processed and read out through the BLW_MAX_AMP register interface.The specific DC-CAN signals to be monitored can be selected by setting dcc_test[6:5] appropriately.dcc_test[6:5] = 00, Input to DC canceller (scaled 1/4).dcc_test[6:5] = 01, Output of IIR1 (scaled 1/4).dcc_test[6:5] = 10, Output of IIR2 (scaled 1/4).dcc_test[6:5] = 11, Output of overall low-pass filter (scaled 1/16).dcc_test[4] dcc_trnsum_en. Override the BLW TRNSUM ouput with the DC-CAN TRNSUM output.In addition to this, the BLW TRNSUM path must be enabled in the TRNSUM block.The specific DC-CAN signals to be accumulated can be selected by setting dcc_test[3:2] appropriately.dcc_test[3:2] = 00, TRNSUM3 = IIR2 acc positive sat count. TRNSUM2 = IIR2 acc negative sat count.TRNSUM1 = IIR1 acc positive sat count. TRNSUM0 = IIR1 acc negative sat count.dcc_test[3:2] = 01, TRNSUM3 = INC/DEC positive sat count.  TRNSUM2 = INC/DEC negative sat count.TRNSUM1 = IIR1 acc positive sat count. TRNSUM0 = IIR1 acc negative sat count.dcc_test[3:2] = 10, TRNSUM3 = INC/DEC positive sat count.  TRNSUM2 = INC/DEC negative sat count.TRNSUM1 = IIR2 acc positive sat count. TRNSUM0 = IIR2 acc negative sat count.dcc_test[3:2] = 00, TRNSUM3 = 0, TRNSUM2 = 0, TRNSUM1 = 0, TRNSUM0 = 0.dcc_test[1:0] dcc_path_sel, Bypass either one or both IIR filter sections in DC canceller feedback loop.dcc_test[1:0] = 11, No LP filter (bypass both IIR sections).dcc_test[1:0] = 10, First-order LP filter (bypass second IIR section).dcc_test[1:0] = 0x, Second-order LP filter (normal operating mode).
 *
 ******************************************************************************/
